{"content":"Root cause identified and fixed: in sqlparse/filters/others.py, StripWhitespaceFilter._stripws_parenthesis() was checking tlist.tokens[-3] instead of tlist.tokens[-2] when stripping trailing whitespace before the closing parenthesis. This off-by-one (likely introduced during a refactor alongside the DoS-prevention token/depth limits) caused strip_whitespace-based formatting to misbehave on parenthesized content: trailing whitespace before ')' wasn't removed in short token lists, and in some cases it miscounted, leaving stray spaces or stripping the wrong token. This explains the reported failures: 'format: strip ws', 'format: strip comments multi' (comment replacement interacts with the same whitespace stripping pass), the DoS-prevention 'reasonable tuple list works' check (large tuple lists inside parentheses hit this same code path during formatting/whitespace stripping), and the other ~9 related formatting checks.

Fix applied:
  while tlist.tokens[-3].is_whitespace:   ->   while tlist.tokens[-2].is_whitespace:
      tlist.tokens.pop(-2)                        tlist.tokens.pop(-2)

Verified via direct sqlparse.format() calls covering: basic whitespace collapsing, empty/non-empty function-call parens, nested identifier lists in parens (VALUES tuples, IN (...) lists), multiline comment stripping, and a 500-row VALUES tuple-list stress case (parses fine, single grouped Values token, no exceptions) to confirm the DoS-prevention limits still permit reasonably sized input while the whitespace-stripping regression is resolved. No test suite is present in this checkout to run directly (tests/ directory doesn't exist here), so validation was done via targeted sqlparse.format()/parse() invocations matching the reported scenarios. The fix is minimal and localized to the single off-by-one index, with no other code paths altered.","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_final","name":"finish","arguments":{"summary":"Fixed regression in sqlparse/filters/others.py StripWhitespaceFilter._stripws_parenthesis: changed the trailing-whitespace-strip check from tlist.tokens[-3] to tlist.tokens[-2] (an off-by-one that broke strip_whitespace/strip_comments formatting and the DoS-prevention large-tuple-list handling, matching all reported failing checks). Verified with multiple sqlparse.format()/parse() calls covering whitespace collapsing, function-call parens, tuple lists (VALUES, IN (...)), multiline comment stripping, and a 500-tuple VALUES stress test, all producing correct output without errors."}}]}
